<title>UK: UK clears FirstBus buy of Great Eastern Rail.</title>
<headline>UK clears FirstBus buy of Great Eastern Rail.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Department of Trade and Industry said on Wednesday it had decided not to refer FirstBus Plc's acquisition of Great Eastern Railway Ltd to the Monopolies and Mergers Commission.</p>
<p>FirstBus said in December last year it had been awarded a seven-year franchise to run Great Eastern, which runs commuter services between London's Liverpool Street station and the suburbs and counties to the east and northeast of the city.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4017</p>
</text>
